BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 676.0 Tm (Why Interviewers Ask This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 650.8 Tm (It is the cheapest possible test of whether you have written code that survived a schema) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 637.3 Tm (migration. A junior says "it returns all columns". A mid-level engineer mentions I/O and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 623.8 Tm (breakage. A senior mentions index-only scans and the API contract between database and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 610.3 Tm (application.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 580.8 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 555.6 Tm (- Saying SELECT * is "slower" without saying why - vague answers read as memorised.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 542.5 Tm (- Claiming it is always wrong. In an ad-hoc query, a COUNT\(*\), or an EXISTS subquery it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 529.4 Tm (is perfectly correct.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 515.9 Tm (- Forgetting that SELECT * inside a view freezes the column list at creation time in some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 502.8 Tm (engines, producing confusing drift later.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 473.3 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 448.1 Tm (- Name every column in application queries; let code review see the contract.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 435.0 Tm (- SELECT COUNT\(*\) is fine - no columns are actually materialised.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 421.9 Tm (- Where a wide row is genuinely needed, define a view or a DTO so the column list lives in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 408.8 Tm (exactly one place.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 379.3 Tm (Follow-up Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 354.1 Tm (1. Is SELECT COUNT\(*\) slower than SELECT COUNT\(1\)? \(No - the planner treats them alike.\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 341.0 Tm (2. What is an index-only scan and how would you verify you got one?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 327.9 Tm (3. How does SELECT * interact with CREATE VIEW and later ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 314.8 Tm (4. Your ORM generates SELECT *. How would you fix that without rewriting every query?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 285.7 Tm (Real-world Scenario) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 260.5 Tm (A team added an internal_notes TEXT column to customers for the support tool. The public) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 247.0 Tm (customer API used SELECT * and serialised whatever it received. The next deploy leaked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 233.5 Tm (internal notes to customers through the JSON response. The fix was one line - an explicit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 220.0 Tm (column list - but the incident was a data-exposure postmortem.) Tj ET
