BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 712.0 Tm (Question 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 679.8 Tm (Difficulty: Easy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 666.2 Tm (Category: SQL -> WHERE vs HAVING) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 636.8 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 611.5 Tm (What is the difference between WHERE and HAVING? Give a query that needs both.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 582.0 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 551.8 Tm (Aspect                WHERE                                HAVING) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 541.6 Tm (-----------------------------------------------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 531.3 Tm (Operates on           individual rows                      groups produced by GROUP BY) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 521.1 Tm (Runs at step          3 \(before grouping\)                  5 \(after grouping\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 510.8 Tm (Aggregates allowed    no                                   yes) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 500.6 Tm (Can use SELECT alias  no                                   in some engines \(MySQL yes, Postgres no\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 490.3 Tm (Typical use           "only delivered orders"              "only customers with more than 2 orders") Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 480.1 Tm (Performance           filters early, less work downstream  filters late, after aggregation cost paid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 457.8 Tm (Rule of thumb: **if the condition can be evaluated by looking at one row, it belongs in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 444.3 Tm (WHERE.** If it needs a COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN or MAX across a group, it belongs in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 430.8 Tm (HAVING.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 412.3 Tm (Both in one query reads naturally as: *"Of the delivered orders only \(WHERE\), show me the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 398.8 Tm (customers who placed more than one \(HAVING\)."*) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 369.3 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 344.1 Tm (Find customers who have more than one delivered order, and their total spend.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 314.6 Tm (Code Example) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 284.4 Tm (SELECT   c.customer_id,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 274.4 Tm (         c.full_name,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 264.4 Tm (         COUNT\(*\)                       AS delivered_orders,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 254.4 Tm (         SUM\(oi.quantity * oi.unit_price\) AS total_spend) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 244.4 Tm (FROM     customers   c) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 234.4 Tm (JOIN     orders      o  ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 224.4 Tm (JOIN     order_items oi ON oi.order_id   = o.order_id) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 214.4 Tm (WHERE    o.status = 'DELIVERED'         -- row-level filter, applied first) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 204.4 Tm (GROUP BY c.customer_id, c.full_name) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 194.4 Tm (HAVING   COUNT\(DISTINCT o.order_id\) > 1 -- group-level filter, applied after) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 184.4 Tm (ORDER BY total_spend DESC;) Tj ET
