BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 345.9 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 320.7 Tm (What is a window function? How does it differ from GROUP BY aggregation?) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 291.2 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 266.0 Tm (A window function computes a value across a set of rows related to the current row while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 252.5 Tm (preserving every input row. GROUP BY collapses rows; a window function annotates them.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 229.0 Tm (GROUP BY                          WINDOW FUNCTION) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 219.0 Tm (-----------------                 -------------------------) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 209.0 Tm (6 rows in                         6 rows in) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 199.0 Tm (2 rows out \(one per group\)        6 rows out \(each + group value\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 189.0 Tm (detail is lost                    detail is kept) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 168.0 Tm (Syntax:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 144.5 Tm (function\(\) OVER \() Tj ET
