BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 637.1 Tm (LAG\(expr, offset, default\) reads a value from a previous row in the window;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 623.6 Tm (LEAD\(expr, offset, default\) reads from a following row. Both require ORDER BY inside) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 610.1 Tm (OVER - "previous" is meaningless without an order.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 591.6 Tm (- offset defaults to 1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 578.5 Tm (- default is returned instead of NULL when the target row does not exist \(first row for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 565.4 Tm (LAG, last for LEAD\). Supplying it is what turns a NULL-riddled result into a clean one.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 546.9 Tm (They replace the classic self-join-on-n-1 pattern, which is both slower and wrong whenever) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 533.4 Tm (the sequence has gaps \(missing months, deleted ids\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 514.9 Tm (Period-over-period growth is the canonical use:) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 491.4 Tm (growth % = \(current - previous\) / previous * 100) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 470.4 Tm (Guard the denominator with NULLIF\(previous, 0\).) Tj ET
