BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 620.1 Tm (is violated even though each transaction was individually correct - write skew.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 590.6 Tm (Code Example) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 560.4 Tm (-- ============ Demonstration of a non-repeatable read ============) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 550.4 Tm (-- Session A                                  | Session B) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 540.4 Tm (BEGIN;                                     -- |) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 530.4 Tm (SELECT balance FROM payments                  -- | ) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 520.4 Tm ( WHERE payment_id = 1;   --> 50000            -- |) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 510.4 Tm (                                              -- | BEGIN;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 500.4 Tm (                                              -- | UPDATE payments SET balance = 40000) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 490.4 Tm (                                              -- |  WHERE payment_id = 1;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 480.4 Tm (                                              -- | COMMIT;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 470.4 Tm (SELECT balance FROM payments                  -- |) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 460.4 Tm ( WHERE payment_id = 1;   --> 40000  \(changed!\) -- |   READ COMMITTED: value changed) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 450.4 Tm (COMMIT;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 433.0 Tm (-- Same script at REPEATABLE READ: the second SELECT still returns 50000,) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 423.0 Tm (-- because the whole transaction sees one snapshot taken at first statement.) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 413.0 Tm (BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 403.0 Tm (SELECT balance FROM payments WHERE payment_id = 1;   --> 50000) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 393.0 Tm (-- ... concurrent committed update happens ...) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 383.0 Tm (SELECT balance FROM payments WHERE payment_id = 1;   --> 50000  \(stable\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 373.0 Tm (COMMIT;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 355.6 Tm (-- ============ Preventing lost update, two correct ways ============) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 345.6 Tm (-- \(a\) Pessimistic: lock the row until commit) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 335.6 Tm (BEGIN;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 325.6 Tm (SELECT balance FROM payments WHERE payment_id = 1 FOR UPDATE;  -- others block here) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 315.6 Tm (UPDATE payments SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE payment_id = 1;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 305.6 Tm (COMMIT;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 288.2 Tm (-- \(b\) Optimistic: make the write itself atomic and conditional) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 278.2 Tm (UPDATE payments) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 268.2 Tm (SET    balance = balance - 100) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 258.2 Tm (WHERE  payment_id = 1) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 248.2 Tm (  AND  balance >= 100;     -- 0 rows affected => rejected, no negative balance) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 230.8 Tm (-- ============ SERIALIZABLE requires a retry loop ============) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 220.8 Tm (BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE;) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 210.8 Tm (-- ... reads and writes ...) Tj ET
