BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 583.4 Tm (This is the senior-level concurrency question. Anyone can list four level names; the signal is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 569.9 Tm (whether you can \(1\) name the anomaly each prevents, \(2\) know your engine's default and its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 556.4 Tm (deviations from the standard, and \(3\) describe the retry requirement of SERIALIZABLE.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 526.9 Tm (Common Mistakes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 501.7 Tm (- Saying Postgres defaults to SERIALIZABLE, or that READ UNCOMMITTED allows dirty reads) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 488.6 Tm (in Postgres. Neither is true.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 475.1 Tm (- Confusing non-repeatable read \(a changed row\) with phantom read \(new rows\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 462.0 Tm (- Choosing SERIALIZABLE without implementing retry on SQLSTATE 40001 - the app then throws) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 448.9 Tm (errors at users under load.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 435.4 Tm (- Assuming SELECT ... FOR UPDATE inside READ COMMITTED prevents phantoms. It locks existing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 422.3 Tm (rows only; new inserts still appear.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 408.8 Tm (- Believing higher isolation fixes bad schema design.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 379.7 Tm (Best Practices) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 354.5 Tm (- Stay at the engine default; raise isolation only for the specific transaction that needs it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 341.4 Tm (- Prefer a conditional UPDATE ... WHERE \(optimistic\) or a version column over row locking -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 328.3 Tm (less blocking, no deadlock class.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 314.8 Tm (- If you use SERIALIZABLE, wrap every transaction in a bounded retry with jitter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 301.7 Tm (- Enforce invariants with constraints as the final backstop: CHECK \(balance >= 0\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 288.6 Tm (- Order writes consistently across the codebase to reduce deadlock probability.) Tj ET
