BT /F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 690.0 Tm (Question 20) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 657.8 Tm (Difficulty: Medium) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 644.2 Tm (Category: SQL -> Security, SQL injection) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 614.8 Tm (Question) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 589.5 Tm (What is SQL injection? Show a vulnerable query, exploit it, and fix it properly.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 560.0 Tm (Answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 534.8 Tm (SQL injection happens when untrusted input is concatenated into SQL text, so the input can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 521.3 Tm (change the structure of the statement rather than only supplying a value. The database cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 507.8 Tm (tell the difference - by the time it parses the string, attacker text is indistinguishable from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 494.3 Tm (developer text.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 475.8 Tm (The only complete fix is to stop building SQL from strings: use **parameterised queries /) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 462.3 Tm (prepared statements**, where the driver sends the SQL template and the values on separate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 448.8 Tm (channels. The value is then never parsed as SQL, no matter what it contains.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 430.3 Tm (Defence layers, strongest first:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 411.8 Tm (1. Parameterised queries - always. This is the actual fix.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 398.8 Tm (2. Allow-listing for identifiers. Table and column names cannot be parameterised, so if a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 385.7 Tm (sort column comes from the user, map it through a dictionary of permitted values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 372.2 Tm (3. Least privilege. The application role should not own the schema or hold SUPERUSER;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 359.1 Tm (injection then cannot DROP TABLE.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 345.6 Tm (4. Input validation as defence in depth - never as the primary control.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.7 Tf 1 0 0 1 66 332.5 Tm (5. Stored procedures help only if they themselves avoid dynamic SQL; EXECUTE inside a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 319.4 Tm (procedure is just as vulnerable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 300.9 Tm (Escaping quotes by hand is not a fix: encodings, numeric contexts, and second-order injection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 287.4 Tm (\(stored data used to build a later query\) all defeat it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 257.9 Tm (Example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 232.7 Tm (A login form and a product search, both built by concatenation.) Tj ET
